<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Twilio voice FALLBACK for the Axiom Gate phone line.

  Twilio requests this only when the primary voice webhook fails: a 5xx, a
  timeout, an unreachable host, or malformed TwiML. On a normal call it is
  never touched.

  IT IS HOSTED HERE, ON CLOUDFLARE PAGES, ON PURPOSE. The primary webhook is
  served from our own infrastructure; a fallback served from the same place
  would be down in every situation that triggers it. This file depends on
  none of that.

  Static hosting cannot answer a POST, so both numbers are configured with
  voice_fallback_method=GET. Switching that back to POST breaks this.

  Keep it plain static TwiML. No Redirect, no callbacks into our own
  infrastructure. Every dependency added here is one more thing that can be
  broken at the exact moment this file is needed.

  (Note for editors: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment and
  makes this file unparseable, which would silently defeat the whole point.)
-->
<Response>
  <Say voice="Polly.Joanna" language="en-US">Thanks for calling Axiom Gate. We're having a technical problem with our phone system right now, and I'm sorry about that. Please leave your name, your number, and a short message after the tone, and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</Say>
  <Record maxLength="120" playBeep="true" trim="trim-silence" finishOnKey="#"/>
  <Say voice="Polly.Joanna" language="en-US">Thanks. We have your message and we'll be in touch. Goodbye.</Say>
  <Hangup/>
</Response>
